{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP11 research/experimentation completed on current origin/main `e29d595b15e1e1073d1770f28ee74fccef8d14e9` and recorded in `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-29.md`.\n\nThe census now covers every production ingress, internal dynamic-loader/cache site, test-loader family, packaging rule, path-sensitive scanner/gate, generated registry, helper script, and documentation class. Key measured scope: 4 persistent host `sys.path` mutations; 3 generic package bootstrappers; 12 generic-loader consumers over 8 implementation modules; 2 additional by-path identity sites; 134 implementation modules; 91 files/329 generic import statements; 38 dynamic/cache-loader files; and 463 Python test files mentioning the generic package. The report calls out the false-green risk in `check_config_ownership.py` after relocation.\n\nDisposable experiments narrowed the implementation: use one installed `rebar.reconciler` implementation namespace plus a two-file subprocess-only `python -m rebar_reconciler` delegating shim. A full package move built and ran from a wheel, preserved stubbed preview/sync contracts, resisted a foreign-package-first hijack, and preserved canonical/legacy help and invalid-mode bytes/exits. The experiments also exposed the real prerequisites: 8 duplicate-source bindings with distinct exception/class identities, 9 hidden mypy errors in 6 files, and 6 path-relocation complexity blockers. A subprocess-RPC alternative would require framing plus new snapshot/env/error contracts and currently conflicts with `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` precedence, so it is outside RP11.\n\nRP11 is revised—not approved. Before implementation it requires: a fresh census at Brant's merged terminal SHA; completion of an architecture-decision lifecycle for reversing the documented subprocess-only package boundary; pre-cutover type/complexity remediation; compatibility oracles installed before relocation; atomic loader/test/scanner/packaging migration; and wheel/source behavior proof. No product/test/config/docs code was changed; only the janitor report and this tracker record were updated."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788130199284873405,"uuid":"4981d234-8dbb-45e4-8545-6b11fa3a8fff"}